[en.FOCUS_C18_000_WATER_IMPROVE]
Stream of Silence Dam

[en.FOCUS_C18_000_WATER_IMPROVE_desc]
The water of the Stream of Silence has a special “silence” effect. On the one hoof, the production of antidotes is heavily dependent on the yield of the stream; on the other hoof, using the stream water to irrigate crops can also have unexpected side effects, such as introversion, aphasia, and even autism tendencies after consumption.\nTherefore, we plan to build dams, canals, and reservoirs in different tributaries of the Stream of Silence to control the confluence of the Stream of Silence with other rivers. On the one hoof, this can improve the purity of the stream water and increase the yield of antidotes; on the other hoof, it can reduce the impact of the stream water on crops.

[en.FOCUS_C18_000_WATER_IMPROVE_TOOLTIP]
The monthly production of the cure that the §YStream of Silence§! can support is increased by §G+50%§!

[zh.FOCUS_C18_000_WATER_IMPROVE]
静默溪大坝

[zh.FOCUS_C18_000_WATER_IMPROVE_desc]
静默溪的溪水具有特殊的“静默”功效，一方面，我们生产解药严重依赖于溪水的产量；另一方面，使用溪水灌溉农作物也会产生意想不到的副作用，例如食用后出现内向、失语症甚至自闭症倾向。\n因此，我们计划在静默溪不同流域修建大坝、运河、与水库，控制静默溪与其他河流的交汇，一方面可以提高静默溪溪水的纯度，提高解药产量；另一方面，可以减少静默溪溪水对农作物的影响。

[zh.FOCUS_C18_000_WATER_IMPROVE_TOOLTIP]
§Y静默溪§!的流量最多能支持的每月解药生产 §G+50%§!

